cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. To cite the dataset specifically, use its own Zenodo DOI (see README); to cite the paper, use the preferred-citation below."
title: "Italian Web Security Study (IWSS)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Manetti"
    given-names: "Giovanni"
    email: "giovanni@perseodesign.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/giovannimanetti11/italian-web-security-study"
url: "https://f-hack.com/analisi-sicurezza-web-italiano-2026"
abstract: >
  A large-scale passive measurement study of the security configuration of
  the Italian web, covering 10,022 .it domains sampled from the Tranco
  top-1M list. Measures HTTP security headers, Content-Security-Policy,
  cookie security attributes, TLS configuration, DNS email authentication
  (SPF, DMARC, DKIM), well-known resources, and CORS configuration using
  exclusively passive, browser-equivalent requests.
keywords:
  - web security
  - security measurement
  - passive scanning
  - HTTP security headers
  - Content-Security-Policy
  - TLS
  - DNS security
  - Italy
  - large-scale measurement study
license: MIT
